{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"nonisolated"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mermaidDiagram"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every state is declared with its description, and with an identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made up from its position among the states, like "},{"code":"state1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A description"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be any text, which an identifier in Mermaid cannot. The states"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected by transitions are connected by an arrow, labeled with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. If several events lead from a state to the same state, they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share one arrow. The initial state has an arrow leading to it from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start, written "},{"code":"[*]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and every ending state has an arrow to the end."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram is the same every time, whatever order the transitions were"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given in, so it can be compared with a saved diagram. This needs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"states to have different descriptions. States with the same description"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are still different states in the diagram, but which of them that gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which identifier can differ."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":"), where ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" is the number of transitions.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The definition of the state machine as a diagram, in the language of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mermaid. It is drawn where Mermaid is, like in Markdown on GitHub, when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"put in a code block marked ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/miamidiagrams\/miamistatemachine\/statemachine\/mermaiddiagram"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MiamiDiagrams\/documentation\/MiamiDiagrams\/MiamiStateMachine\/StateMachine\/mermaidDiagram","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MiamiDiagrams\/documentation\/MiamiDiagrams","doc:\/\/MiamiDiagrams\/documentation\/MiamiDiagrams\/MiamiStateMachine","doc:\/\/MiamiDiagrams\/documentation\/MiamiDiagrams\/MiamiStateMachine\/StateMachine"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mermaidDiagram","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"extendedModule":"MiamiStateMachine","title":"mermaidDiagram","modules":[{"relatedModules":["MiamiStateMachine"],"name":"MiamiDiagrams"}],"conformance":{"constr